#include "AnimMcpTools.h"

#include "Bridge/AnimMcpDispatcher.h"
#include "Bridge/AnimMcpTypes.h"
#include "Core/AnimMcpCapture.h"

// AI 애니 생성 Phase 8-2 — 대상 메시 캡처 (Core/AnimMcpCapture). 애셋을 만들지 않고 CaptureOutputRoots 아래 새 폴더에 PNG 만 쓴다.
namespace AnimMcpTools
{
	void RegisterCaptureTools(FAnimMcpDispatcher& Dispatcher)
	{
		Dispatcher.RegisterTool(TEXT("capture_animation"),
			TEXT("Capture an AnimSequence on a target skeletal mesh as PNG images (no assets created; Phase 8-2 — judge a retarget without opening Persona). Params: asset (AnimSequence), mesh (SkeletalMesh compatible with the asset's skeleton — always explicit, else BAD_REQUEST reason SKELETON_MISMATCH), facing ('+Y' | '-Y' | '+X' | '-X' — the UE axis the mesh's front looks along; Vesper +Y), output_dir (absolute, a NEW or empty folder below [AnimGraphMcp] CaptureOutputRoots — else OUTPUT_PATH_NOT_ALLOWED reason CAPTURE_ROOT / BAD_REQUEST OUTPUT_DIR_NOT_EMPTY), times?[] (seconds on the clip, 1..12) | count? (1..12, default 4 — first and last frame included; not both: CONFLICTING_FIELDS), views? (['front','side'] default both), cell_height_px=512, max_aspect=2.0, margin=0.08, bounds_max_samples=600, sheet_max_px=3000 (same rules as the Blender source-skeleton review.render, so the two sheets line up), supersample=2 (1..3), label? (prefix of every cell label), sequence? ({fps=15 (1..30), cell_height_px=320, start?, end?, max_frames=150} — one image per time with the views side by side, for an animated image; null = none), compare? ({label?, rows: [[image, …] per sheet row]} — images under ImportSourceRoots (e.g. the Blender source-skeleton frames of the same times) appended as extra columns into compare.png), attachments? ([{mesh (SkeletalMesh — reference pose — or StaticMesh), socket | bone (exactly one, on the captured mesh or its skeleton — SOCKET_NOT_FOUND / BONE_NOT_FOUND / CONFLICTING_FIELDS), offset? {location[3], rotation[pitch, yaw, roll], scale[3]} (relative to the socket/bone)}] ≤ 4 — e.g. a weapon; rendered and included in the framing; the caller composes game attach data such as AttachTransform · AttachOffset into one offset), lighting? ({exposure_bias, key, fill, sky} — advanced), max_seconds=120 (the sequence stops there: warning CAPTURE_TRUNCATED). Camera rules: orthographic; front = from in front of the body (body's left on screen right), side = from the body's right (front on screen right); framed ONCE on the whole clip (≤ bounds_max_samples frames + the rows) — the mesh LOD0 vertices boxed per dominant bone and moved by each frame's bone transforms — so travel and height changes show; fixed cell height, width = range ratio (1/max_aspect..max_aspect), floor (z = 0) always visible as a strip. Scene = a transient preview world: the mesh (single node, SetPosition → RefreshBoneTransforms; cloth simulation off), an unlit backdrop and floor, a key light from the camera's upper left (shadows) + fill + the thumbnail ambient cubemap; SceneCapture2D FinalColorLDR with Lumen, SSR, TAA, motion blur, bloom, eye adaptation and DOF off, manual exposure. Result {asset, mesh, facing, length, frame_rate, frames_total, dir, frames[{row, time, frame, frame_time, view, path, sha1 (pixels), subject_px{x0,y0,x1,y1}|null, coverage_pct, touches_edge}], sheet (rows = times, columns = views), compare{path, label, own_columns, compare_columns, size, scale}|null, sequence{dir, fps, count, frames[], times[], size, truncated, seconds}|null, layout{rows[{time, frame, frame_time, clamped}], columns[], cell_height, gap, size, scale}, camera{view: {look, right, ortho_width_cm, ortho_height_cm, resolution, cm_per_px}}, bounds{min, max, frames_sampled, from, boxed_bones}, attachments[{mesh, class, socket, bone, offset{location, rotation, scale}, local_bounds_cm{min, max}}], render{…}, cells_touching_edge, seconds}. A capture must leave no package dirty (else UNEXPECTED_DIRTY — the files stay, details.dir). Render/readback/write failures → CAPTURE_FAILED (details.reason). The images show the raw sequence on the mesh: no weapon unless attachments, no cloth/hair physics, no AnimBP layers (IK, aim) — a human judges them."),
			[](FAnimMcpContext& Context, FAnimMcpError& OutError) -> TSharedPtr<FJsonObject>
			{
				return AnimMcpCapture::Capture(Context, OutError);
			});
	}
}
